    "text": "Date: March 15, 2026Time: 1 p.m. ETVenue: Paycom CenterTV: ABCStreaming: Check local listingsRadio: Sports Animal 98.1, 830 WCCOBuy tickets: Buy Timberwolves at Thunder tickets on StubHubTwo dominant guards in Shai Gilgeous-Alexander and Anthony Edwards are getting ready to go toe-to-toe. The Oklahoma City Thunder's homestand will continue as they prepare to take on the Minnesota Timberwolves at 1:00 p.m. on Sunday at Paycom Center. The Thunder's defense has only allowed 107.8 points per game this season, so the Timberwolves' offense will have their work cut out for them.AdvertisementThat Thunder defense was on full display on Thursday, rewarding bettors who took the risk on the low 215.5-point over/under. They snuck past the Celtics with a 104-102 win.Gilgeous-Alexander continued his habit of posting crazy stat lines, almost dropping a double-double with 35 points and 9 assists. The game marked Gilgeous-Alexander's second in a row with at least 35 points.Meanwhile, the Timberwolves finally caught a break after three consecutive losses. They walked away with a 127-117 victory over the Warriors on Friday.AdvertisementEdwards produced another solid performance, going 13-for-22 en route to 42 points in addition to 8 rebounds and 5 assists. The game also marked Edwards' 14th in a row with at least one steal. Another player making a difference was Rudy Gobert, who nearly posted a double-double with 18 points and 9 rebounds.Oklahoma City now sits at a stellar 52-15 record this season. As for Minnesota, their win bumped their record up to 41-26.Looking ahead, the Thunder are the favorite in this one, as the experts expect to see them win by 8.5 points. This contest might not be the best time to bet them against the spread since they've let bettors down the last seven times they've played.AdvertisementMinnesota Timberwolves at Oklahoma City Thunder Odds, Line and SpreadBetting lines as of 03/15/2026 at 7:49 AM ET. Odds subject to change.Moneyline (ML): Thunder 